e everybody I said you know just like  I started out saying you know what's  ball so it was a black women in my class  and was you know it was my friends who  kind of knew where Oklahoma was all of  those things were things that helped me  to get through it and whether or not  you're going into a male-dominated  question whether you're going to a file  a complaint you really have to go into  this with a understanding of how you're  going to be supportive because I haven't  ever come across any woman who is my age  or even reasonably younger who hasn't  needed that support I haven't run across  a person of color who has it needed that  support because of some of the sometimes  open hostilities and sometimes just  microaggressions that they experience  and you need somebody that you couldn't  be able to talk to about what that is  like so finding that support system  whatever it is and I'm very fortunate  because I had it I can say I have no  regrets now because that's what I have  and that's what I continue to have right  this is a question from a student in the  class of 2018 this person says this room  appears to have fewer younger students  than most the elements I thought it said  fewer younger people and I was going to  say present company notwithstanding but  fewer younger students than most the  elements do you think or what do you  think young people misunderstand about  the history of sexual misconduct and  sexual harassment I think people do you  know I'm not surprised that younger  people don't have any idea who I am I  really I I'm on a college campus trust  me  and and I think that we have a very  different idea of what history is what  recent history is the older we are than  younger people they win but I think I'm  probably not the person to ask what  young people why young people are not  present or what their understanding is I  think we but I would love to have that  conversation not just because they I  want them to come to see me but because  I th